Rule 1 (input tensor must have rank at least 2 and all positive dimensions; prevents "Shape (...) must have rank at least 2" and negative/zero dims)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 2 (fft_length as tensor must be a 1-D tensor of length 2; prevents "fft_length must have shape [2]" and index errors)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 2
>>
Rule 3 (fft_length elements must be positive when provided as tensor; prevents negative dimension errors)
{v_2 : tensor} |= min(v_2) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (fft_length provided as a Python tuple must have exactly two positive integers; prevents index errors and negative dimensions)
{v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len = 2 ∧ v_2[0] ≥ 1 ∧ v_2[1] ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (last two dimensions of input must not exceed fft_length when fft_length is a tuple; reduces shape mismatch/cropping issues)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2.len = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) ≤ v_2[0] ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≤ v_2[1] + 1
>>
Rule 6 (restrict name to a scalar string to avoid ambiguous truth-value errors)
{v_3 : str} |= v_3 = "none"
>>
Rule 7 (use exactly 2-D input to avoid broadcasting/incompatible shape operations with fft_length of length 2; prevents "Incompatible shapes: [...] vs. [2]")
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 2
